I need to understand the specific problem better. The task mentions "porous-medium traveling-wave profiles" and references methods_brief.txt. I need to create code to solve the traveling-wave ODE for porous media. First, let me check if there are any related work files or additional data.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "find . -type f -name \"*.txt\" -o -name \"*.md\" -o -name \"*.pdf\""
  }
}
```

Let me try a different approach to explore the workspace structure.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir /s /b"
  }
}
```

Now I need to understand the porous medium equation and its traveling wave reduction. The porous medium equation is typically: ∂u/∂t = Δ(u^m) where m > 1. For traveling waves, we look for solutions of the form u(x,t) = f(ξ) where ξ = x - ct. This reduces to an ODE boundary value problem.

Let me create the necessary directory structure and start implementing the solution.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "mkdir code outputs report report\\images"
  }
}
```

Now I need to install necessary Python packages and run the code.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python -m pip install numpy scipy matplotlib"
  }
}
```

Now let me run the code to see if it works.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python porous_traveling_wave.py"
  }
}
```

I need to fix the string escaping issue. The backslashes in LaTeX need to be raw strings or double backslashes.

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/porous_traveling_wave.py",
    "old_str": "            plt.xlabel('$\\xi = x - ct$')\n            plt.ylabel('$f(\\xi)$')",
    "new_str": "            plt.xlabel(r'$\\xi = x - ct$')\n            plt.ylabel(r'$f(\\xi)$')"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/porous_traveling_wave.py",
    "old_str": "            plt.title(f'Traveling wave profile (m={m}, c={c})')",
    "new_str": "            plt.title(f'Traveling wave profile (m={m}, c={c})')"
  }
}
```

Actually, I need to fix all the LaTeX strings. Let me check and fix them systematically.

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/porous_traveling_wave.py",
    "old_str": "    plt.subplot(2, 2, 4)\n    plt.xlabel('$\\xi$')\n    plt.ylabel('Residual')\n    plt.title('ODE residuals')",
    "new_str": "    plt.subplot(2, 2, 4)\n    plt.xlabel(r'$\\xi$')\n    plt.ylabel('Residual')\n    plt.title('ODE residuals')"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/porous_traveling_wave.py",
    "old_str": "    plt.xlabel('$\\xi = x - ct$')\n    plt.ylabel(\"$f'(\\xi)$\")",
    "new_str": "    plt.xlabel(r'$\\xi = x - ct$')\n    plt.ylabel(r\"$f'(\\xi)$\")"
  }
}
```

